From 7e8d92cff09efce1170b6e0af054f6920f01288c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viljo Marrandi <30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:03:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(verify): a lateral rapid is re-read against the stock's
 top under it

The rapid-in-stock law caps every column at the stock's highest point.
#1091 (PR #1098) re-reads a convicted vertical dive against the stock
and part solids under the tool stack; lateral rapids kept the flat cap,
so a drill's link at its retract plane across the low part of a stepped
"from model" stock was convicted as if the boss stood under it, and the
post was blocked.

acquit_by_stock_top now re-reads an upright lateral rapid the same way:
each band of the stack over the capsule it sweeps along the move,
against the highest stock or part facet within its radius, the tip at
the rapid's lowest end. It only removes convictions and fails closed as
the dive does. A dive is the zero-length capsule (dist2_seg_tri of a
point is dist2_tri), so its verdicts are unchanged.

Pinned by stepped_stock_link (a part-sourced drill's link over the low
step passes and posts; across the boss, or with the boss under the rim
along the way, it is convicted and blocks the post) and the stock_top
unit tests (traverse acquitted, crossing the boss, boss under the rim,
holder band, part, fail-closed). #1098's
only_upright_column_dives_are_re_read now expects its diagonal dive
acquitted, and posed still convicted.

Stacked on #1098.

Fixes #1095

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
